    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0792" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/5–1749</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of Financial and
                        Development Policy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knapp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-05-26">May 26, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I concur in the recommendations contained in jour memorandum to me of May 17,
                    1949 with only one reservation. That is, while it may be desirable to withdraw
                    certifications if Chinese funds are being improperly dissipated, I do not
                    believe we should make a firm decision to do so without further consideration of
                    the various implications of such action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">alton</hi>] B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">utterworth</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
